Our practice investment of the day is a weekly hold on Costco wholesale corporation,

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:17.240
ticker KOST on the NYSE. The catalyst is bared reiterating its outperform rating after robust

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:24.420
June same-store sales that exceeded expectations. Technical setup shows price action above the 50-day

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:30.080
moving average with volume tracking near the 20-day average. Nearest support sits at the

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:37.000
recent swing low. We set a stop loss 6% below entry to limit drawdown if consumer spending weakens

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:45.100
further. The 5-day target is plus 3% to plus 6% if sales momentum holds. Confidence level

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:51.300
is medium because the sales catalyst and analyst support are aligned, but broader retail sector

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:57.780
volume confirmation is still needed. This setup demonstrates how to use an analyst re-iteration as

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:04.140
a secondary filter rather than a primary signal, forcing us to verify volume and sector breadth

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:10.700
before committing capital. Listeners learn to treat upgrades as confirmation tools instead of stand

00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:16.900
alone triggers. Now, here's something that most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:23.000
before I figured it out. Imagine you added a REIT position to your TFSA last month,

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:29.440
expecting steady distributions while home prices stalled. Your order filled cleanly, yet the actual

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.880
economics depend on whether the trust uses mortgage debt, property level leverage, or both.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:41.940
Publicly traded REITs such as Ryokan or Canadian apartment REIT trade with daily liquidity but

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:48.020
distribute most taxable income, creating immediate tax drag inside non-registered accounts.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.820
Mortgage investment corporations offer higher yields through private lending, yet carry liquidity

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:59.880
risk, and different tax treatment as interest income. The professionals always check the distribution

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:07.140
composition and debt to gross book value ratio before allocating, because a 60% payout ratio

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:12.660
funded by new unit issuance is not the same as one backed by rising rental cash flow.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.440
The biggest mistake with real estate exposure is treating every vehicle as equivalent to owning

00:05:18.440 --> 00:05:24.340
physical property. Instead, always match the structure to your account type and time horizon.

